<h2>MT4 vs MT5: Which Should GCC Traders Use?</h2>
<p>MT4 is best for forex and CFD traders who want simplicity, a large EA library, and proven stability. MT5 offers more asset classes (stocks, futures), more timeframes, and faster backtesting. If you trade primarily forex and CFDs, MT4 is the proven choice. Our guide <a href="/guides/mt4-vs-mt5-vs-ctrader">MT4 vs MT5 vs cTrader</a> covers this in detail.</p>',
 '[{"q":"Which brokers offer MT4 in UAE?","a":"All major brokers reviewed on Trader Gulf offer MetaTrader 4 for UAE traders, including Exness, XM, Pepperstone, IC Markets, and AvaTrade. MT4 is available on desktop, web browser, iOS, and Android."},{"q":"Is MetaTrader 4 available in Arabic?","a":"Yes. MetaTrader 4 supports an Arabic interface with right-to-left text display. You can change the language in the platform settings. All brokers serving the GCC region fully support MT4 in Arabic."},{"q":"Can I use Expert Advisors (EAs) on MT4 in GCC?","a":"Yes. MT4 supports automated trading via Expert Advisors. All brokers listed above allow EA trading on their MT4 platforms. You can use free and paid EAs from the MetaTrader marketplace."},{"q":"Is MT4 free for Gulf traders?","a":"Yes. MetaTrader 4 is free to download and use. You simply need an account with an MT4-compatible broker. There are no additional platform fees — the broker earns through spreads and commissions."}]',
 '[1,2,3,4,5,7,11,12]',
