-- Low Spread MENA
('best-low-spread-forex-brokers-mena', 'category',
 'Best Low Spread Forex Brokers for MENA Traders 2025',
 '<p>Spread costs are one of the biggest determinants of trading profitability. We compare the brokers offering the lowest EUR/USD spreads available to traders in the Middle East and North Africa.</p>',
 '<h2>Why Low Spreads Matter for MENA Traders</h2>
<p>Every time you open and close a trade, you pay the spread — the difference between the buy and sell price. For active traders in GCC and MENA, choosing a low-spread broker can save hundreds of dollars per month. IC Markets, Pepperstone, and Exness consistently offer some of the lowest spreads available globally, with EUR/USD spreads as low as 0.0 pips on raw/ECN accounts.</p>
<h2>Raw/ECN vs Standard Accounts for MENA Traders</h2>
<p><strong>Standard accounts</strong> embed the spread into the price, with no separate commission. EUR/USD spreads of 0.8–1.2 pips are typical. Good for beginners and low-frequency traders.</p>
<p><strong>Raw/ECN accounts</strong> offer near-zero spreads (0.0–0.3 pips) but charge a commission per lot, typically $3–$6 per standard lot per side. Better value for active traders opening more than 20–30 trades per month.</p>
<h2>How We Measure Spreads</h2>
<p>We track live EUR/USD spreads during the London/New York overlap (8:00–17:00 GMT), which is the period of maximum liquidity and tightest spreads. Spreads widen during low-liquidity periods — always check your broker''s spread schedule before trading major news events.</p>',
 '[{"q":"Which broker has the lowest spread in MENA?","a":"IC Markets and Pepperstone consistently offer the lowest spreads for MENA traders, with EUR/USD raw spreads from 0.0 pips. Exness also offers ultra-low spreads on its Zero account. All three are available to traders across the GCC and MENA region."},{"q":"What is a good EUR/USD spread?","a":"A EUR/USD spread of below 1.0 pip is considered competitive on a standard account. Raw ECN accounts should offer 0.0–0.3 pips plus commission. Anything above 1.5 pips on a standard account is above average."},{"q":"Do low spread brokers offer Islamic accounts?","a":"Yes. IC Markets, Pepperstone, and Exness all offer Islamic swap-free accounts alongside their low-spread raw/ECN accounts. You can combine the lowest spreads with Sharia-compliant trading."},{"q":"Are low spread brokers safe for MENA traders?","a":"Yes. The brokers listed above are regulated by top-tier regulators including ASIC (Australia), FCA (UK), and CySEC (Cyprus). Low spreads do not compromise safety — these are established, well-capitalised brokers."}]',
 '[3,1,4,2,9,5,6]',
 'Best Low Spread Forex Brokers MENA 2025 | Trader Gulf',
 'Compare forex brokers with the lowest EUR/USD spreads for MENA traders. Raw ECN accounts, 0.0 pip spreads, Islamic accounts. Expert comparison 2025.',
 1),

-- Islamic Accounts GCC
('best-islamic-forex-brokers-gcc', 'category',
 'Best Islamic Forex Brokers in GCC 2025',
 '<p>Swap-free Islamic forex accounts allow Muslim traders to participate in currency markets without incurring overnight interest (riba). We have reviewed every major broker''s Islamic account offering for GCC traders.</p>',
 '<h2>What is an Islamic Forex Account?</h2>
<p>An Islamic forex account, also known as a swap-free account, is designed for Muslim traders who wish to trade in compliance with Sharia law. The key feature is the elimination of overnight interest (swap) charges, which are considered riba (interest) and are prohibited under Islamic finance principles. Instead, some brokers charge an administration fee after a holding period.</p>
<h2>How Islamic Accounts Work</h2>
<p>When you hold a currency position overnight in a conventional forex account, you pay or receive a swap (overnight interest). In an Islamic account, this swap is replaced by either: (1) No overnight charge at all (true swap-free); (2) A flat administration fee after 3–7 days; or (3) A wider spread to compensate. The best Islamic accounts charge no fees at all for typical overnight positions.</p>
<h2>Are All Islamic Accounts the Same?</h2>
<p>No. The quality of Islamic accounts varies significantly between brokers. Some brokers offer genuine swap-free accounts with no hidden charges. Others charge excessive administration fees that effectively replicate swap costs. Always read the Islamic account terms carefully before opening an account.</p>
<h2>Best Islamic Accounts Compared</h2>
<p>Based on our testing: <strong>Exness</strong> offers the most transparent Islamic account — true swap-free with no administration fees on most instruments. <strong>XM</strong> offers Islamic accounts with a 7-day holding period before fees apply. <strong>Pepperstone</strong> provides Islamic accounts on all account types with no additional charges for standard holding periods.</p>',
 '[{"q":"Which GCC broker has the best Islamic account?","a":"Exness is widely considered to offer the best Islamic swap-free account for GCC traders — no administration fees on most instruments, available on all account types, and no minimum holding period before the swap-free status applies."},{"q":"Is Islamic forex trading permissible?","a":"Many Islamic scholars permit swap-free forex trading as long as the exchange is instantaneous (spot settlement) and no riba (interest) is charged. However, opinions vary between scholars, and we recommend consulting your religious authority for personal guidance."},{"q":"Are Islamic forex accounts free?","a":"True swap-free accounts with no additional fees are offered by Exness and Pepperstone. Some brokers charge administration fees after a holding period of 3–7 days. Always check the specific terms of the Islamic account before opening."},{"q":"Can I use an Islamic account with a demo?","a":"Yes. Most brokers allow you to test their Islamic account features on a demo account before committing real funds. This lets you verify that no overnight charges are applied."}]',
 '[2,1,3,4,5,8,6,14]',
 'Best Islamic Forex Brokers GCC 2025 — Halal Trading | Trader Gulf',
 'Compare the best Islamic swap-free forex brokers for GCC traders. Sharia-compliant, no riba, no overnight interest. Expert reviews 2025.',
 1)

